---
layout: null
permalink: /search.json
---
{%- comment -%}
The full article text is indexed on purpose, so search can find a phrase
buried in the middle of a post rather than only matching titles and
abstracts.

That makes this file grow with the archive - a deliberate trade, because
search.js no longer requests it on page load. It is fetched once, on the
first keystroke in the search box, so its size costs nothing to a reader
who never searches. Revisit only if the fetch itself becomes slow;
capping `content` with `truncatewords` is the lever.

`normalize_whitespace` collapses the runs of blank lines that strip_html
leaves behind. It saves little but keeps the payload free of filler.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
  {% assign all_posts = '' | split: '' %}
  {% assign all_posts = all_posts | concat: site.reflections %}
  {% assign all_posts = all_posts | concat: site.natural-sciences %}
  {% assign all_posts = all_posts | concat: site.arts-literature %}
  {% assign all_posts = all_posts | concat: site.contemporary %}
  {% assign all_posts = all_posts | concat: site.social-sciences %}
  {% for post in all_posts %}
    {
      "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ post.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
      "abstract": {{ post.abstract | jsonify }},
      "content": {{ post.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | jsonify }},
      "date": {{ post.date | date: "%B %-d, %Y" | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]